<h2>Frame transitions: <c>transition=</c></h2>

<p>
  By default a frame <b>morphs</b> from the previous one. Put <c>transition=</c> on a <c><frame></c> to change
  how <i>that</i> frame is entered:
</p>

<ul>
  <li><c>morph</c> (default) — the diff animation</li>
  <li><c>fade</c> — no matching: the old code fades out, the new code fades in</li>
  <li><c>none</c> — a hard cut, no animation at all</li>
</ul>

<p>Frame 1 is the starting point; the next three use a different mode each.</p>

<code lang=typescript id=g1>
  <frame>
    function area(w: number, h: number) {
      return w * h;
    }
  </frame>
  <frame>
    function area(width: number, height: number) {
      return width * height;
    }
  </frame>
  <frame transition=fade>
    function area(width: number, height: number) {
      return width * height * 2;
    }
  </frame>
  <frame transition=none>
    function area(width: number, height: number) {
      return width * height * 3;
    }
  </frame>
  <frame>
    function area(width: number, height: number) {
      return width * height * 4;
    }
  </frame>
</code>

<notes>
  Per frame option, written on the frame you are entering. Default is morph.
</notes>
